    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0904" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg768"/>

                <head>No. 540.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 14,
                        1887</date>.<lb/>(Received September 14, 1887.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you herewith
                    a memorandum calling the attention of the United States Government to certain
                    points in the report made by Lieutenant Schwatka, of the U. S. Army, of a
                    reconnaissance made by him in Alaska, and to observe at the same time that he
                    traversed British territory for a considerable distance without any intimation
                    having been given to the British authorities of his intention of so doing. I may
                    add, however, that Her Majesty’s Government do not attach any importance to this
                    fact, and that no doubt had their acquiescence been asked it would not have been
                    refused.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                            West</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d540-a1.xml" xpointer="d540-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
